 "notes": "A flat, machine-read form: answers are printed in its boxes, dates and numbers one character to a cell. Answers: the mailing and Hawaii addresses are 'street, city, ST ZIP'; 'Same' leaves line 7 blank, as the form asks only for a different location. A fiscal year is 'Fiscal year ending: MM/DD'. Owners are 'Last, First M.I.; title; residential address; phone' (up to two; a separate sheet for more). Withholding 'Yes: date' ticks 22a with the date wages begin; the general excise license ticks 22b GET/Use with its filing period and start date, and line 24 lists the GE location. Left for the applicant: every FEIN/TIN/SSN choice and number for the owners in line 20 (Placetta never writes an SSN), lines 17 to 19 (parent corporation), the other tax types on page 2, the fees due and the total on line 21 ($20 for the GE license), and the signature and date. Mailed with the fee to the Department of Taxation, or the same application made online at hitax.hawaii.gov.",
